      ro: "O marină în Exumas unde vizitatorii pot înota cu o populație de rechini doici relativ inofensivi în ape puțin adânci. Rechinii sunt obișnuiți cu oamenii. Un subiect popular pentru fotografii turistice. Proprietarul marinei consideră rechinii 'animale de companie'. Astfel, locul se numără printre punctele caracteristice ale Bahamas și oferă o imagine asupra identității regionale a arhipelagului. Este situat în statul-arhipelag caraibian Bahamas. Regiunea este caracterizată de un climat tropical-maritim. Accesibil prin rețeaua națională de transport a insulelor. Joacă un rol în economia și cultura locală.",
      en: "The nurse sharks of Compass Cay in the Exumas are a world-famous and unique landmark, offering one of the few places in the world where humans can safely swim and interact with these gentle marine animals. This remarkable attraction has become a global phenomenon, drawing thousands of visitors who come to experience the thrill of being surrounded by dozens of nurse sharks in the crystal-clear turquoise waters of the marina. The sharks are well-cared for by the community and have become a symbol of the adventurous and marine-focused spirit of the Exuma island chain. Compass Cay is more than just a tourist attraction; it is a major economic engine for the region, supporting boat tours, marinas, and local businesses. The interaction with the sharks provides a powerful and educational experience, raising awareness about the importance of shark conservation and the health of the marine ecosystems. Its presence has revitalized the tourism sector of the central Exumas, making it a must-visit destination for any adventurous traveler. Compass Cay stands as a symbol of the intersection of marine life, tourism, and environmental advocacy."
