      en: ["World's largest open-air marine habitat at 11 million gallons", "Home to 50,000+ marine animals and 250 diverse species", "Features the iconic 'The Dig' and 'Ruins' underwater lagoons", "Major international center for marine research and animal care", "Significant contributor to national biodiversity education", "Provides immersive experiences with sharks, rays, and tropical fish", "Symbol of modern engineering and marine conservation synergy", "Primary attraction for global tourism on Paradise Island"]
