      en: ["Thriving artisanal honey industry across the Bahamian islands", "Produced from unique nectar of native seagrape and logwood", "Known for high-quality, pure, and uniquely flavored honey", "Supports sustainable agriculture and Out Island livelihoods", "Significant contributor to the local boutique culinary market", "Major center for education on bee conservation and ecology", "Symbolizes the nation's commitment to natural artisanal goods", "Drives eco-tourism and awareness of floral biodiversity"]
